  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">G2G Sustainable Urban Rural Economic Development Kenya: inception</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SURED project aims to achieve the following objectives:1.	Provide technical assistance to selected counties and stakeholders for coordinating their County Integrated Development Plans and Strategic Economic Development Plans. The project will demonstrate how to translate these plans into Spatial Plans that are economically, ecologically, and socially viable.2.	Demonstrate the implementation of the Spatial, Business, and Financial Investment Instruments, Plans, and Processes necessary for developing two regionally focused urban planning Pilot Projects. These projects will be centered around the development of an Agro-Industrial-Business park, inspired by the Dutch Greenport and Metropolitan Food Cluster concepts, using a multi-sectoral inclusive approach.3.	Foster a positive and mutually reinforcing relationship between counties, cities, and rural areas. Cities should provide rural areas with markets and facilities, while rural areas should provide cities with food security and essential ecosystem services.4.	Enhance urban-rural linkages across the continuum of space, place, and economics. This will harness the transformative power of urbanization for sustainable development.5.	Unlock government-to-business and business-to-business opportunities while strengthening the position of the Dutch Alliance of Sustainable Urban Development in Africa (DASUDA) and other Dutch companies, enterprises, and coalitions within the Urban Development and Spatial Planning (sub)sectors in Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
